# Bulwark Webmail 1.8.0 standalone tarball SHA-256.
# Source: https://github.com/bulwarkmail/webmail/releases/tag/1.8.0
#   asset: bulwark-standalone-1.8.0-linux-amd64.tar.gz
# Captured 2026-08-08 directly from the GitHub release artifact.
# 1.8.0 (2026-08-06): fixes the stale account chip after mailbox impersonation
# (bulwarkmail/webmail#697, GH #646) — the handoff now drops the browser-cached
# account list so the top-left chip follows the impersonated mailbox.
#
# Bulwark ships a prebuilt "standalone" Next.js tarball (server.js +
# node_modules + .next), so we no longer git-clone + `npm ci` +
# `npm run build`. install_bulwark() downloads this tarball, verifies
# the SHA below, and extracts it.
#
# To re-capture on a version bump (BOTH the version in install.sh AND this
# checksum must change together — a version bump alone fails SHA verification):
#   curl -sSL https://github.com/bulwarkmail/webmail/releases/download/<v>/bulwark-standalone-<v>-linux-amd64.tar.gz | sha256sum
# Paste the returned 64-char hex below. install.sh `_die`s if the
# placeholder PLACEHOLDER_CAPTURE_ON_FIRST_DEPLOY survives.
df4f5f215735ef1768ed54c3e6b516ea7b3352add19a9f9f6627cf8c48529de4
